Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their purpose for this task  

bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr  
• geo_id : 5–digit county FIPS code – join key to the vaccination table  
• total_pop : latest (2018 5‑year ACS) population – denominator for the rate  

bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all  
• facility_place_id : unique identifier of every vaccination site – what we count  
• facility_sub_region_2_code : 5–digit county FIPS code – join key to the ACS table  
• facility_sub_region_1 : state name (‘California’) – state filter  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'        -- limit to California  
• WHERE geo_id LIKE '06%'                           -- limit ACS rows to California  
• GROUP BY facility_sub_region_2_code               -- aggregate by county  

Ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries  
(Each returns ≤ 20 rows to illustrate the data.  Replace ✱ with the columns shown.)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few California counties in the ACS table
--    Verify geo_id’s format and population figures
SELECT geo_id, total_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
WHERE geo_id LIKE '06%'      -- ‘06’ = California
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List distinct state names that appear in the vaccination table
--    Confirm the exact spelling for California
SELECT DISTINCT facility_sub_region_1
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Look at vaccination rows for California, with their county FIPS codes
SELECT facility_place_id, facility_name, facility_sub_region_2_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. How many distinct vaccination sites are in the whole state?
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) AS sites_statewide
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California';
```

```sql
-- 5. Sample: count the sites for 20 California counties
SELECT facility_sub_region_2_code AS county_fips,
       COUNT(DISTINCT facility_place_id) AS site_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
GROUP BY county_fips
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Compare population and site count for a single county (e.g., Alameda 06001)
SELECT a.geo_id,
       a.total_pop,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id) AS site_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`  AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` AS v
  ON a.geo_id = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE a.geo_id = '06001'     -- Alameda County
GROUP BY a.geo_id, a.total_pop;
```

```sql
-- 7. Check whether every California county in ACS appears in the vaccination file
SELECT a.geo_id
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`  a
LEFT  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` v
       ON a.geo_id = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE  a.geo_id LIKE '06%'          -- California
GROUP BY a.geo_id
HAVING COUNT(v.facility_place_id)=0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute “sites per 1,000 people” for 20 counties (quick test)
SELECT a.geo_id AS county_fips,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id)                       AS site_cnt,
       a.total_pop,
       1000 * COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id) / a.total_pop  AS sites_per_1k
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`  a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` v
  ON a.geo_id = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE a.geo_id LIKE '06%'               -- California counties only
GROUP BY county_fips, a.total_pop
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Rank California counties by sites per 1,000 population (top 20 shown)
SELECT a.geo_id                                        AS county_fips,
       a.total_pop,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id)             AS site_cnt,
       ROUND(1000 * COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id) / a.total_pop, 2)
                                                     AS sites_per_1k
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`  a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` v
  ON a.geo_id = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE a.geo_id LIKE '06%'            -- California only
GROUP BY county_fips, a.total_pop
ORDER BY sites_per_1k DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: number of vaccine sites per 1,000 people
--     for every county in California
SELECT a.geo_id                                AS county_fips,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id)     AS site_count,
       a.total_pop,
       ROUND(1000 * COUNT(DISTINCT v.facility_place_id) / a.total_pop, 3)
                                               AS sites_per_1000_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`            a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all` v
  ON a.geo_id = v.facility_sub_region_2_code
WHERE a.geo_id LIKE '06%'                      -- restrict to California counties
GROUP BY county_fips, a.total_pop
ORDER BY county_fips
LIMIT 20;
```

